// "Draws" (EventFilter kind) = a player drew ([CR#121.1]). Mirrors
// event/GainsLife's shape (a player-identity subject via
// `filter::recipient_phrase`, no `~` shorthand). Mind the underlying event:
// the body expands to `Drawn`, not `Draws` — `Draws` is only this macro's
// own name (the `PlayerAction`-kind macro of the same name, "draws N
// cards", is a completely different expansion; macro names are namespaced
// per-kind, so the two coexist without conflict).
// Usage: Draws(who) — e.g. Draws(Ref(You)), Draws(OpponentOf(Ref(You))).
(
    name: "Draws",
    template: "${0} draw a card",
    kinds: [EventFilter],
    params: [Predicate],
    body: Drawn(who: Param(0)),
)
